  "_comment": [
    "The single place where AI model IDs live, for both the viewer (viewer/ts/profile.ts) and the coz script (coz plot's /optimize endpoint and coz suggest-points).",
    "Providers retire model IDs regularly. To keep that from breaking coz:",
    "  * Every model ID coz knows about is defined here and nowhere else (tests/test_models.py enforces this).",
    "  * 'retired' maps known-dead IDs to replacements; saved viewer selections and --model arguments are migrated through it.",
    "  * When a provider rejects a model as unknown, the request is retried with a same-family replacement picked from the provider's live list.",
    "  * scripts/update_models.py (run weekly by .github/workflows/update-models.yml) checks 'models' against each provider and opens a PR when one disappears.",
    "OpenAI requests use Chat Completions, which the -pro models reject, so they are not listed.",
    "Bedrock serves current Claude models only through inference profiles; the global. profiles route to any region."
